{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/925097-john-s-scion-fate-binding-rules","id":925097,"title":"John's Scion Fate Binding rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-02T16:32:53-07:00","id":925097,"title":"John's Scion Fate Binding rules","content":"As the topic name says I'm having an issue with reading John's fate binding rules. From my understanding, you roll the scions legend in sets for each point of legend but I'm having issues with a few things. (this case the scion in question is legend 5, spent 3 legend in a village of about 150 in the Egyptian dessert using the ward boon 3 times in quick succession)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The issue is that now that my player's scions are demi-gods when they get fate bonded shouldn't those bindings become cults since many people saw his actions instead of one? If so what should I do with the fate binding roles if the binding is strong enough? Does the whole cult get the role?<br /> <br /> I would appreciate any clarifications or advice anyone has because I'm aren't sure on how to make heads or tales about some of these rules are written. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T22:42:35-07:00","id":925225,"title":"","content":"This is probably not the advice you want, but almost everyone I know tosses out their Fate system.<br /> <br /> JSR has written a lot of really great things, especially their pantheon overhauls and writeups. I stand by their research being top quality, and their website was beautiful even with the wide-hip Genzoman art. But their Fate system is both confusing and a huge amount of bookwork once you figure it out. I cannot recommend using it.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/fate\" target=\"_blank\">Scion 2.0 has an easy one.</a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.thecbg.org/wiki/index.php?title=Fate_Expectations_%28Lost_Atlanta%29\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Lost Atlanta has an okay one.</b></a><br /> Modern Mythos never really published theirs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:51:44-07:00","id":925676,"title":"","content":"Oh really? Is it worse than the canon system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T22:19:25-07:00","id":926278,"title":"","content":"It essentially means that if your Scions do anything obviously cool, they will probably end up fatebound to mortals who will, through the power of their own belief, alter and re-write that Scion to match their [i.e. your] expectations. It takes a lot of the fun out of the whole game for anyone who is expecting to play larger-than-life characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 07-05-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T01:20:18-07:00","id":926322,"title":"","content":"Their Fate system tries to turn everybody into a caricature, with all or nothing stats. You can spend experience to slow or stop that, but it feels like a penalty instead of a fun game mechanic. Also, our storyteller said that it was too hard to keep track of everything.<br /> <br /> But they made some other cool stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:11:29-07:00","id":926449,"title":"","content":"Oh, they did lots of great stuff. But fatebinding wasn't one of the good ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:19:56-07:00","id":926485,"title":"","content":"I've talked to that group and even they admit that they had entire binders dedicated to tracking Fatebonds. It is a HUGELY complex system. I can't recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}